  "final_message": "I have started checking the repository status.\nI am checking the repository structure and will examine the files shortly.\nI am listing the workspace files to see the project layout.\nI am searching the codebase for references to ARCH-4.\nI am checking for references to channel across the codebase.\nI am checking references to channel in the test suite.\nI am running the test suite to establish a baseline.\nI am waiting for the test suite to complete.\nI am running `npm test` to verify the initial baseline.\nI have launched `npm test` and am awaiting the result.\nI am waiting for the initial test execution to complete.\nThe test run is currently executing. I'll evaluate the results as soon as it completes.\nI'll wait for the tests to finish.\nI am checking the git commit history.\nI am checking git history details.\nI am checking for other branches and tags in the repository.\nI am running `npm run arch` to verify dependency-cruiser rules.\nI am waiting for `npm run arch` to complete.\nI'll check the arch check result once it completes.\nI am waiting for the architecture check to finish.\nI'll wait for the dependency-cruiser run to complete.\nI'm waiting for the dependency-cruiser check to complete.\nI am awaiting the architecture check output.\nI'll wait for the task to finish.\nI will wait for the command to finish.\nI cannot remove the `channel` field from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates architecture rule **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/GEMINI.md#L27):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Key Considerations\n\n1. **External Contract Compatibility**: [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is published to Kafka and consumed across repository boundaries by external services (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Removing the `channel` field would introduce a breaking contract change for deployed consumers.\n2. **Deprecation Requirement**: According to ARCH-4, changes to domain events must be additive. Any removal or rename of existing fields must follow a formal deprecation process across consumers before the field can be removed.\n3. **Core Model Dependency**: In [`src/core/events.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59), [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/events.ts#L42) maps `order.channel` directly onto the event payload (`channel: order.channel`). Removing `channel` from [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) would break this event mapping as long as `OrderPlaced` requires the field.\nThe previous background checks have finished. As noted above, removing `channel` from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) directly violates architecture rule **ARCH-4** in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/GEMINI.md#L27). Please let me know if you would like to initiate a deprecation path or make other changes that preserve backward compatibility.\n",
